  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Massachusetts has $13.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 75,777 awards with an average award size of $182K. Obligations are down 28.5% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in the state, obligating $10.7B so far this fiscal year. Historical annual totals show variability: FY21 totaled $24.2B, FY22 totaled $17.9B, FY23 totaled $18.3B, FY24 totaled $17.8B, FY25 totaled $19.3B, and FY26 totaled $13.8B to date. Engineering and aerospace-related work make up a large share of spending: Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounts for $2.9B, Engineering Services accounts for $1.6B, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) accounts for $1.2B. RAYTHEON COMPANY leads vendors with $3.3B in obligations, followed by GENERAL ELECTRIC COMPANY with $1.3B and an additional RAYTHEON COMPANY entries at $1B, $479M, and $443M among other top suppliers.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did federal obligations in Massachusetts change year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 28.5% year over year. Fiscal totals show a peak of $24.2B in FY21 and a partial FY26 total of $13.8B. Fiscal-year totals were $17.9B in FY22, $18.3B in FY23, $17.8B in FY24, and $19.3B in FY25."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate federal contracting in Massachusetts?",
        "body": "Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing is the largest industry with $2.9B. Engineering Services accounts for $1.6B and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) accounts for $1.2B. RAYTHEON COMPANY is the largest vendor with $3.3B, followed by GENERAL ELECTRIC COMPANY with $1.3B and MASSACHUSETTS INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY with $873M."
      }
    ]
  },
